#%PAM-1.0
#
# Unlocking the screen, on a Debian-family system. wlrix-lock runs this stack as the logged-in
# user, under the service name `wlrix-lock`, to check the password of the account whose session
# it locked -- nobody else's.
#
# Only auth and account: a locker re-proves who is at the keyboard, it does not open a session.
# pam_unix checks the password through its setuid helper `unix_chkpwd`.

@include common-auth
@include common-account
